From 2c55ce82137ae01ede58782f38c0568dfeb588a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Gonzalez <dev@gonzalezerik.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:05:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Add the gem and ohci PCI drivers for the iBook G3

Import if_gem.c, if_gem_pci.c, if_gemreg.h and if_gemvar.h from
freebsd/sys/dev/gem and ohci_pci.c from freebsd/sys/dev/usb/controller
so a powerpc NewWorld machine gets its built-in Sun GEM/Apple GMAC
Ethernet and its Open Host Controller Interface as PCI drivers.  The
gem files carry the usual RTEMS adaptations: the bus method
descriptors come from the rtems/bsd/local headers and the MAC address
comes from rtems_bsd_get_mac_address instead of Open Firmware.

Declare a dev_nic_gem module and turn it on in the default buildset
next to the other NIC modules, build ohci_pci.c as part of
dev_usb_controller, add the RTEMS_BSD_DRIVER_PCI_GEM reference macro
and the nexus-devices list for the ibookg3 BSP: the legacy pcib with
gem, miibus, ukphy, ohci, usbus, uhub and umass.

Verified on QEMU mac99 with the ibookg3 BSP: gem0 gets a DHCP lease
and passes TCP in both directions, ohci0 enumerates a USB keyboard
whose keystrokes read back through /dev/ukbd0, and umass0 attaches a
USB mass storage device.
